From: kschen <admin@kschen.eu.org>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 21:14:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8996pro-xiaomi-capricorn: set sound
 card model

The "sound" node inherited from msm8996-xiaomi-common.dtsi has no "model"
property, and capricorn - unlike gemini, natrium and scorpio - never
overrides it.  qcom_snd_parse_of() leaves card->name NULL in that case and
snd_soc_register_card() then bails out:

  platform sound: deferred probe pending: msm-snd-apq8096: MultiMedia1: \
      error getting cpu dai name
  msm-snd-apq8096 sound: probe with driver msm-snd-apq8096 failed with error -22

so the device comes up with no sound card at all ("No soundcards found").
The deferred-probe message is just the normal EPROBE_DEFER while the APR
DAIs are still coming up; the -EINVAL is the real failure.

Add the missing model, matching the other three Xiaomi msm8996 boards.

With this, card 0 registers with six playback and six capture PCMs and the
full WCD9335 mixer control set.

Signed-off-by: kschen <admin@kschen.eu.org>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996pro-xiaomi-capricorn.dts | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996pro-xiaomi-capricorn.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996pro-xiaomi-capricorn.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996pro-xiaomi-capricorn.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996pro-xiaomi-capricorn.dts
@@ -107,6 +107,10 @@
         firmware-name = "qcom/msm8996/capricorn/slpi.mbn";
 };
 
+&sound {
+	model = "capricorn";
+};
+
 &venus {
         firmware-name = "qcom/msm8996/capricorn/venus.mbn";
 };
